[14.09599, "o", "1. Use the openai-community/gpt2 model as the base model for fine-tuning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096004, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.096098, "o", "2. Implement LoRA fine-tuning with the following configuration:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096116, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[14.096139, "o", "> "]
[14.096159, "o", "   - LoRA rank (r): 8\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096196, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>    - LoRA alpha: 16\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096228, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[14.096254, "o", "> "]
[14.096298, "o", "   - Target modules: ['\"'\"'c_attn'\"'\"'] (attention layers)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096322, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.096414, "o", "3. Train the model using the provided training and validation sets\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096422, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.096523, "o", "4. Save your training script to /app/train_lora.py for verification\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096543, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[14.096556, "o", "> "]
[14.096647, "o", "5. Save the trained LoRA adapter to /app/experiments/lora_adapter, including:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096667, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.096724, "o", "   - adapter_config.json (LoRA configuration)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096739, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.096813, "o", "   - adapter_model.safetensors (LoRA weights)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096825, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[14.096837, "o", "> "]
[14.096902, "o", "   - tokenizer_config.json (tokenizer configuration)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.096914, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.097084, "o", "   - adapter_config should include default arguments including '\"'\"'base_model_name_or_path'\"'\"' and '\"'\"'task_type'\"'\"' \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.097112, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.097233, "o", "6. It is recommended to use the PEFT (peft==0.15.0) library for implementing LoRA fine-tuning.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[14.097244, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[14.097357, "o", "7. Create a results file at /app/lora_results.json with the exact schema below\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
